  "name": "Email a weekly Google Maps rank heatmap with GeoGridAPI and Gmail",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "c0ea4323-3d27-5c6b-b91f-2cfc300b504a",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -520,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Weekly Google Maps rank heatmap by email\n\nEvery Monday, this workflow measures where a business ranks on Google Maps for a keyword, on every point of a grid around it (a local SEO \"geo-grid\"), then emails you the heatmap with the key figures: average rank, points in the top 3, points in the top 20, change since last week and the competitors ranking ahead.\n\n### How it works\n1. The schedule starts the workflow every Monday at 08:00.\n2. **Run geo-grid** sends the business, keyword and grid size to the GeoGridAPI REST API.\n3. The grid takes 20 seconds to 2 minutes: the workflow checks it every 20 seconds until it is completed. A failed grid stops with an error and its credits are refunded.\n4. **Download heatmap image** gets the 1200 x 1092 PNG map and **Write the email** builds the message.\n5. **Email the report** sends it with Gmail.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a free account on [geogridapi.io](https://geogridapi.io) (500 free credits) and create an API key. `gga_test_` keys are free and return sample grids, good for a first run.\n2. Add a **Header Auth** credential named `GeoGridAPI key`: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer gga_live_...`. Select it in the three HTTP Request nodes.\n3. Connect your Gmail account.\n4. Fill in **Settings**: business (\"name, city\"), keyword, grid size (3, 5, 7 or 9), radius in km, language and recipient.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Cost: 1 credit per point, so a 7 x 7 grid is 49 credits a week.\n- Swap Gmail for Slack, Outlook or Telegram: the image is in the binary field `data`.\n- Several clients? Duplicate the workflow or read them from a Google Sheet."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
